# The panel registry. THIS FILE IS THE ENUMERATION.
#
# One row per display-popup binding in .tmux.conf. tests/integ/panel_conformance.bats
# asserts CLOSURE in both directions: every popup bind has a row here, and every row here
# has a popup bind. That is what makes panel coverage structural -- a panel added without a
# row FAILS the fast tier, rather than being silently uncovered.
#
# Why a manifest at all, when .tmux.conf already lists the binds? Because .tmux.conf cannot
# say what a panel IS. `kind` is the case in point: bind g points at $HOME/.local/bin/
# agent-panel, a cargo-installed Rust binary that is not a tracked file, so a naive
# "$HOME/ -> repo root, then stat it" check fails on it and on nothing else.
#
# COLUMNS -- read by name, never by position (panel_field), so inserting one mid-row cannot
# silently shift an assertion. Keep the header comment's names in sync with the rows.
#
#   table     the tmux key table: root, or whatever -T names
#   key       the bound key, as .tmux.conf spells it
#   kind      script      a tracked, executable file in this repo
#             bin-symlink a .local/bin symlink into .local/src (dispatch alias)
#             rust-bin    a cargo-installed binary; only its crate is in the repo
#   geometry  the TARGET class: FULL | WIDE | SMALL (panel_geometry_class)
#             Several panels do not sit at their target yet; the geometry ratchet counts
#             them down. .tmux.conf is normalised to %hidden constants in one late pass,
#             deliberately AFTER every script draws its own --border, so adding -B can
#             never leave a surface frameless.
#   path      repo-relative path to the file the tests read
#   argv      arguments the bind passes, or - for none
#
# table key   kind         geometry path                                  argv
root    f     script       WIDE     .local/src/tmux/sessionizer.sh        -
root    R     script       WIDE     .local/bin/sessions                   search --window
root    H     bin-symlink  WIDE     .local/src/tmux/servers.sh            pick
root    A     script       FULL     .local/src/tmux/scratch.sh            open #{q:pane_current_path}
root    g     rust-bin     FULL     .local/src/agent-panel                -
root    C-g   script       FULL     .local/src/tmux/fleet.sh              -
root    P     script       WIDE     .local/src/tmux/pr-viewer.sh          -
root    p     script       WIDE     .local/src/tmux/projects.sh           -
root    y     script       FULL     .local/src/tmux/questions.sh          -
tags    l     bin-symlink  SMALL    .local/src/tmux/tags.sh               ls
root    W     bin-symlink  SMALL    .local/src/tmux/tags.sh               pick
root    K     script       WIDE     .local/bin/keys                       -
